/-!
# Cubic words for all even seven-point double cosets

For each of the 49 even representatives in the existing double-coset
exhaustion, a word in that representative and the standard Sylow subgroup
has cube one. A second word recovers the representative using this cubic
word and the Sylow subgroup. The equations are checked by kernel reduction.
Consequently any alternating overgroup of the standard Sylow subgroup lies
in every subgroup containing the Sylow subgroup and its cubic elements.
This includes nonsolvable overgroups and the whole alternating group.

The reproducible word data is in `source/generate.py` and `source/words.json`.
Source application: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.49(l) and its point stabilizers on printed pp.1144–1145.
-/

